4
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:23,460
And it's actually a little more complicated than we would like it to be, but what else

5
00:00:23,460 --> 00:00:24,680
is new?

6
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:29,000
So let me share my screen with you because I want to show you something.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,420
And here's what I want to show you.

8
00:00:32,420 --> 00:00:39,120
What we want to think about when someone is at a place and they have dementia, and we'll

9
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:42,140
call it home because it should feel like home.

10
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:45,680
It should be a place where I want to be and feel like I should be.

11
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:51,660
And whether it's home in a traditional sense or not, that's really secondary here.

12
00:00:51,660 --> 00:00:55,860
But the questions we want to ask are three.

13
00:00:55,860 --> 00:00:58,980
Number one, can I get to the thing?

14
00:00:58,980 --> 00:00:59,960
I want to do?

15
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:05,060
Can I get to the task, to the pieces that I need to do the task?

16
00:01:05,060 --> 00:01:06,460
Can I get there?

17
00:01:06,460 --> 00:01:09,860
Can I physically get there?

18
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:12,720
Number two, am I safe?

19
00:01:12,720 --> 00:01:14,460
Does it make sense that I'm doing this?

20
00:01:14,460 --> 00:01:22,140
Do I have the skill sets that are needed that make it from the outside or majority wise,

21
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:26,440
or at least as far as a risk profile, make it reasonable?

22
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:28,400
And three is, can I act?

23
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:30,480
Can I actually accomplish it?

24
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:31,480
Can I do it?

25
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:37,280
Do I have the skills that I need within me to do the thing I want to do?

26
00:01:37,280 --> 00:01:43,560
And if that's the case, if it all comes together and I have the desire, I do it.

27
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:48,920
The tricky part is all of these pieces of the puzzle start shifting around on me and

28
00:01:48,920 --> 00:01:51,280
shifting around on you, quite honestly.

29
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:56,120
And so when we say, can I do it for myself?

30
00:01:56,120 --> 00:01:58,360
The answer is probably not the way I used to.

31
00:01:58,360 --> 00:02:02,680
Even early on, not the way I used to.

32
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:07,060
So I'm having to learn new things, do it a different way, but so are the people who are

33
00:02:07,060 --> 00:02:08,500
trying to support me.

34
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:11,960
And there are things we can do with the environment and the setup to make it better.

35
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:16,220
So I thought we might actually look at some of the components that people don't always

36
00:02:16,220 --> 00:02:17,220
think about.

37
00:02:17,220 --> 00:02:23,000
I want to go to the part that we don't think so much about, which is how aware of the situation

38
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:26,800
and my skills, my changing skills, am I?

39
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:28,240
So it's situational.

40
00:02:28,240 --> 00:02:29,240
It's a matter of awareness.

41
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:31,240
How aware am I?

42
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:35,420
Because the more aware I am, the better probability I'll be safe.

43
00:02:35,420 --> 00:02:37,600
And if I do do something, I'll do it well.

44
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:41,280
And I'll also know where things are and how to access them and make use of them because

45
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:44,840
I've done some compensatory things or someone has.

46
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:50,600
So with sapphires, we tend to sustain our awareness skills, although sometimes it's

47
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:54,040
tough for us to think things through and things still surprise us.

48
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:57,560
With diamonds, when you're in a diamond state, your old emotions and your old, you know,

49
00:02:57,560 --> 00:02:57,640
your old emotions are going to be a little bit different.

50
00:02:57,640 --> 00:02:57,760
So I'm going to go to the next slide.

51
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:57,800
So I'm going to go to the next slide.

52
00:02:57,800 --> 00:02:57,860
So I'm going to go to the next slide.

53
00:02:57,860 --> 00:02:57,940
So I'm going to go to the next slide.

54
00:02:57,940 --> 00:02:58,000
So I'm going to go to the next slide.

55
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:00,980
And these old abilities sort of drive your new interactions.

56
00:03:01,280 --> 00:03:06,000
So suddenly it may surprise me that I'm having trouble or it may frustrate me.

57
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:10,320
Emeralds, well, that's where we have that time travel thing going on.

58
00:03:10,420 --> 00:03:14,020
So sometimes the situation I think I'm in isn't actually a situation I'm in.

59
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:17,680
So that makes me a definite higher risk category.

60
00:03:18,300 --> 00:03:20,000
And ambers, it's all about sensation.

61
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:22,580
And so it's really not about thinking.

62
00:03:22,700 --> 00:03:24,760
It's about what do I like or what don't I like.

63
00:03:24,760 --> 00:03:27,760
And safety wise, I'm not as aware of the situation.

64
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:30,240
from the external point of view.

65
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:32,920
Rubies, only in moments.

66
00:03:33,040 --> 00:03:34,460
I'm a lot less body aware.

67
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:38,020
And so my skill sets, my fine motor skills,

68
00:03:38,260 --> 00:03:41,240
I may not know what I don't know,

69
00:03:41,320 --> 00:03:44,660
or I may, and I may come and seek assistance.

70
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:46,100
So it varies.

71
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:49,780
And pearls, I tend to be more inside aware

72
00:03:49,780 --> 00:03:50,760
than outside aware.

73
00:03:50,760 --> 00:03:54,100
So situation-wise, I don't know I'm hungry,

74
00:03:54,200 --> 00:03:55,840
and I'm actually not feeling that.

75
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:57,980
I'm not thirsty, or maybe I am,

76
00:03:58,020 --> 00:03:59,620
and I don't know how to communicate it.

77
00:04:00,340 --> 00:04:02,440
So situation varies.

78
00:04:03,020 --> 00:04:04,940
Now, let's talk about safety.

79
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:07,920
Well, the problem is with safety, it all depends.

80
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:11,160
So that's the one people tend to think about.

81
00:04:11,340 --> 00:04:13,700
So here's the quick version for me.

82
00:04:14,200 --> 00:04:16,520
Sapphires, if you have it, you use it.

83
00:04:16,580 --> 00:04:18,080
So you sustain whatever you've got.

84
00:04:18,140 --> 00:04:19,040
You wanna keep it going.

85
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:20,440
But if you're safe, you're safe.

86
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:22,460
If you're not, you never have been,

87
00:04:22,660 --> 00:04:23,820
and you've had lots of accidents.

88
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:25,820
Diamonds, typically,

89
00:04:25,940 --> 00:04:27,120
you need a second set of eyes

90
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:29,320
because about 50% of the time,

91
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:31,520
you may be inaccurate related to the skills

92
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:32,400
you have in that moment.

93
00:04:33,300 --> 00:04:36,880
Emeralds, probably benefit from a friendly preset,

94
00:04:37,100 --> 00:04:39,300
prompts, reduce the risk,

95
00:04:39,760 --> 00:04:42,520
check out mistakes, modify in the moment.

96
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:43,920
So you need somebody around,

97
00:04:44,020 --> 00:04:45,480
not interfering, but present.

98
00:04:46,400 --> 00:04:48,860
Ambers, 24-7, you need somebody

99
00:04:48,860 --> 00:04:50,260
to sort of watch the environment,

100
00:04:50,440 --> 00:04:52,320
watch the task, keep an eye on the person

101
00:04:52,320 --> 00:04:55,460
to make sure what is happening is safe,

102
00:04:55,460 --> 00:04:55,820
safe for you.

103
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:56,820
And then you need somebody

104
00:04:56,820 --> 00:04:58,820
to monitor the individual and make sense for the individual

105
00:04:58,820 --> 00:05:00,820
because in that moment, it's just a moment,

106
00:05:00,820 --> 00:05:02,820
and be able to back up and try again.

107
00:05:02,820 --> 00:05:06,820
Rubies, eyes on with an arm's reach pretty much all the time

108
00:05:06,820 --> 00:05:10,820
because of the variation in ability and inability.

109
00:05:10,820 --> 00:05:14,820
And pearls, we need somebody in immediate space 24-7.

110
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:16,820
So that's safety monitoring.

111
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:17,820
Doesn't mean you interfere,

112
00:05:17,820 --> 00:05:19,820
but it means you're present and accounted for,

113
00:05:19,820 --> 00:05:21,820
and you're present in every sense.

114
00:05:21,820 --> 00:05:23,820
Then we get to access.

115
00:05:23,820 --> 00:05:24,820
Well, how accessible are things?

116
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:25,820
Well, how accessible are things?

117
00:05:25,820 --> 00:05:26,820
Can people get to them?

118
00:05:26,820 --> 00:05:29,820
With sapphires, you can actually consider hidden access.

119
00:05:29,820 --> 00:05:31,820
You sort of know where you keep things

120
00:05:31,820 --> 00:05:32,820
or where things can be put,

121
00:05:32,820 --> 00:05:35,820
or the person that you're living with,

122
00:05:35,820 --> 00:05:36,820
not just for yourself.

123
00:05:36,820 --> 00:05:37,820
So you know where they are,

124
00:05:37,820 --> 00:05:41,820
but they can't get to them unless you want that to happen.

125
00:05:41,820 --> 00:05:43,820
Diamonds, we may have emergency controls

126
00:05:43,820 --> 00:05:45,820
when monitoring is impossible

127
00:05:45,820 --> 00:05:48,820
and the person has varying awareness.

128
00:05:48,820 --> 00:05:51,820
Emeralds, we probably need to control over access

129
00:05:51,820 --> 00:05:53,820
unless we're monitoring during critical pieces.

130
00:05:53,820 --> 00:05:54,820
You can't just turn people to the side.

131
00:05:54,820 --> 00:05:55,820
You can't just turn people loose

132
00:05:55,820 --> 00:05:57,820
because they possibly could,

133
00:05:57,820 --> 00:05:58,820
but they very possibly couldn't,

134
00:05:58,820 --> 00:06:01,820
and they may or may not know that.

135
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:05,820
Ambers, we want to control what we want people to have access to,

136
00:06:05,820 --> 00:06:09,820
but we also have to offer what they do like to do.

137
00:06:09,820 --> 00:06:13,820
And then rubies, supported access or no access,

138
00:06:13,820 --> 00:06:16,820
but we've got to manage the environment and access.

139
00:06:16,820 --> 00:06:19,820
Access to steps, access to outdoors,

140
00:06:19,820 --> 00:06:22,820
access to hot, to cold, to food, to drink.

141
00:06:22,820 --> 00:06:23,820
Everything has to be managed.

142
00:06:23,820 --> 00:06:25,820
And it's a big job.

143
00:06:25,820 --> 00:06:28,820
And then with pearls, we need supported provision.

144
00:06:28,820 --> 00:06:30,820
And if we don't give them access,

145
